-- Chapter 1: Physical divisions of Assam
State Profile, Office of the Chief Minister of Assam: https://cm.assam.gov.in/state-profile$t$, date '2026-11-24' from public.content where slug = $t$physical-divisions-of-assam$t$ on conflict do nothing;
The Barak Valley: a small {{term:valley}} in the south, about 40 to 50 km in average width and length.
The Karbi Anglong and Dima Hasao (North Cachar) hills: they lie between the two valleys, with an average height of 300 to 400 metres, rising to almost 2,000 metres.$t$ from public.content where slug = $t$physical-divisions-of-assam$t$ on conflict do nothing;
